{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/dao/stream/slice_peer.cljc | sed -n '1,360p'; nl -ba test/dao/stream/slice_test.clj | sed -n '1,420p'; nl -ba test/dao/stream/slice_test.cljs | sed -n '1,420p'; nl -ba shadow-cljs.edn | sed -n '1,80p'; nl -ba bb.edn | sed -n '1,50p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.stream.slice-peer\n     2\t  \"Process B of the DaoStream v2 Phase 5 slice.\n     3\t\n     4\t   Phase 5 is deliberately two operating-system processes rather than two\n     5\t   compositions in one: a same-process socket test cannot show that a\n     6\t   descriptor is self-contained, nor that no accidental shared state carries\n     7\t   identity across.  This namespace is therefore a whole peer program, not a\n     8\t   fixture — `dao.stream.slice-test` (JVM) and `dao.stream.slice-test`\n     9\t   (Node) each spawn it as a child process and speak to it only over pipes.\n    10\t\n    11\t   The bootstrap channel is explicit and load-bearing: B receives A's\n    12\t   descriptor as Transit JSON *text* in `argv`, decodes it through the\n    13\t   contract's descriptor gate, and never receives a handle, an atom, or any\n    14\t   other host value from A.  Everything else is a line-oriented Transit\n    15\t   command/reply protocol on stdin/stdout, so the parent observes B only\n    16\t   through data B chose to report.\n    17\t\n    18\t   Two properties of the composition here are the point of Phase 5's fourth\n    19\t   fact and must not be `refactored' away:\n    20\t\n    21\t   * the deposit medium and its `:dao.stream/newest` cursor are minted once,\n    22\t     before the first `attach!`, and survive every attachment; and\n    23\t   * the cursor is never handed to `attach!` and never used through the\n    24\t     WebSocket handle, which has no reader surface at all.\n    25\t\n    26\t   This peer owns its own cadence.  It installs no timer and polls nothing:\n    27\t   host socket callbacks deposit into the medium on their own threads (JVM) or\n    28\t   turns (Node), and the parent asks for what has accumulated with `:events`.\"\n    29\t  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n    30\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    31\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\n    32\t            [dao.stream.transit :as transit]\n    33\t            [dao.stream.ws :as ws]\n    34\t            ;; `:cljd` first and empty: the ClojureDart host-eval pass also\n    35\t            ;; matches `:clj`, so a `:clj` branch reached first would try to\n    36\t            ;; require a JVM-only namespace.  cljd has no peer build.\n    37\t            #?@(:cljd []\n    38\t                :clj [[dao.stream.ws.jvm :as host]]\n    39\t                :cljs [[dao.stream.ws.node :as host]]\n    40\t                :default [])))\n    41\t\n    42\t\n    43\t(def admission\n    44\t  \"The deposit declaration for B's traffic medium.  Declared as configuration\n    45\t   provenance, never interrogated from the handle.\"\n    46\t  {:retention :evict-oldest :capacity 256 :value-domain :portable-values})\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\t(defn- emit!\n    50\t  \"Write one reply as a single line of Transit JSON on stdout.\"\n    51\t  [value]\n    52\t  (let [text (transit/encode value)]\n    53\t    #?(:clj (do (println text) (flush))\n    54\t       ;; shadow's :node-script target does not install a print-fn that is\n    55\t       ;; guaranteed to reach stdout unbuffered; write the stream directly.\n    56\t       :cljs (.write js/process.stdout (str text \"\\n\"))\n    57\t       :default nil)))\n    58\t\n    59\t\n    60\t(defn- exit!\n    61\t  []\n    62\t  #?(:clj (System/exit 0)\n    63\t     :cljs (.exit js/process 0)\n    64\t     :default nil))\n    65\t\n    66\t\n    67\t(defn- buffer\n    68\t  []\n    69\t  (:dao.stream/handle (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n    70\t                                     ring/capacity-key 256})))\n    71\t\n    72\t\n    73\t(defn make-peer\n    74\t  \"Compose B's boundary around one bootstrapped descriptor.\n    75\t\n    76\t   Ordering matters and is asserted by the parent: the medium exists and its\n    77\t   cursor is minted before any `attach!`, so no deposited event can outrun the\n    78\t   position the parent will later resume from.\"\n    79\t  [descriptor]\n    80\t  (let [traffic (buffer)\n    81\t        minted (stream/cursor traffic stream/anchor-newest)\n    82\t        attacher (ws/make-attacher\n    83\t                   {:traffic {:dao.stream/handle traffic\n    84\t                              :dao.stream/surface #{:writer}}\n    85\t                    :admission admission\n    86\t                    :connect! #?(:cljd nil :clj host/connect! :cljs host/connect!\n    87\t                                 :default nil)})]\n    88\t    (atom {:descriptor descriptor\n    89\t           :traffic traffic\n    90\t           :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor minted)\n    91\t           :attacher attacher\n    92\t           :handle nil\n    93\t           :attach nil})))\n    94\t\n    95\t\n    96\t(defn- drain\n    97\t  \"Read forward from the kept cursor without consuming: reads are\n    98\t   non-destructive, so this returns the events and the position after them.\"\n    99\t  [state]\n   100\t  (loop [cursor (:cursor state)\n   101\t         events []]\n   102\t    (let [result (stream/next (:traffic state) cursor)]\n   103\t      (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\n   104\t        (recur (:dao.stream/cursor result) (conj events (:dao.stream/value result)))\n   105\t        [cursor events (:dao.stream/outcome result)]))))\n   106\t\n   107\t\n   108\t(defn handle-command!\n   109\t  \"Interpret one parent command and emit exactly one reply.\"\n   110\t  [peer command]\n   111\t  (let [state @peer\n   112\t        handle (:handle state)]\n   113\t    (case (:cmd command)\n   114\t      :attach\n   115\t      ;; The descriptor is the bootstrapped one every time, so a reattachment\n   116\t      ;; provably uses the identical portable value, not a repaired copy.\n   117\t      (let [result ((:attacher state) (:descriptor state))]\n   118\t        (swap! peer assoc :handle (:dao.stream/handle result) :attach result)\n   119\t        (emit! {:reply :attach\n   120\t                :outcome (:dao.stream/outcome result)\n   121\t                :attachment (:dao.stream/attachment result)}))\n   122\t\n   123\t      :append\n   124\t      (emit! {:reply :append\n   125\t              :outcome (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! handle (:value command)))})\n   126\t\n   127\t      :close\n   128\t      (emit! {:reply :close\n   129\t              :outcome (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/close! handle))})\n   130\t\n   131\t      :surfaces\n   132\t      (emit! {:reply :surfaces :value (stream/declared-surfaces handle)})\n   133\t\n   134\t      :handle-descriptor\n   135\t      (let [result (stream/descriptor handle)]\n   136\t        (emit! {:reply :handle-descriptor\n   137\t                :outcome (:dao.stream/outcome result)\n   138\t                :descriptor (:dao.stream/descriptor result)\n   139\t                :identity (:dao.stream/identity result)}))\n   140\t\n   141\t      :events\n   142\t      (let [[cursor events outcome] (drain state)]\n   143\t        (swap! peer assoc :cursor cursor)\n   144\t        (emit! {:reply :events :events events :outcome outcome}))\n   145\t\n   146\t      :exit\n   147\t      (do (emit! {:reply :exit}) (exit!))\n   148\t\n   149\t      (emit! {:reply :unknown :cmd (:cmd command)}))))\n   150\t\n   151\t\n   152\t(defn- feed!\n   153\t  \"Split a stdin chunk into whole lines, returning the unterminated remainder.\"\n   154\t  [peer pending chunk]\n   155\t  (let [parts (str/split (str pending chunk) #\"\\n\" -1)]\n   156\t    (doseq [line (butlast parts)\n   157\t            :when (not (str/blank? line))]\n   158\t      (handle-command! peer (transit/decode line)))\n   159\t    (last parts)))\n   160\t\n   161\t\n   162\t(defn -main\n   163\t  \"Bootstrap from `argv` and serve the parent's commands until told to exit.\"\n   164\t  [& args]\n   165\t  (let [descriptor (transit/decode-descriptor (first args))\n   166\t        peer (make-peer descriptor)]\n   167\t    (emit! {:reply :ready :descriptor descriptor})\n   168\t    #?(:clj\n   169\t       ;; Blocking on stdin is safe here: every socket callback runs on a host\n   170\t       ;; thread and deposits into the medium without this loop's help.\n   171\t       (loop []\n   172\t         (when-let [line (read-line)]\n   173\t           (when-not (str/blank? line)\n   174\t             (handle-command! peer (transit/decode line)))\n   175\t           (recur)))\n   176\t\n   177\t       :cljs\n   178\t       ;; Node has one thread, so stdin must be a turn on the event loop or the\n   179\t       ;; socket callbacks would never run.\n   180\t       (let [pending (atom \"\")]\n   181\t         (.setEncoding js/process.stdin \"utf8\")\n   182\t         (.on js/process.stdin \"data\"\n   183\t              (fn [chunk] (reset! pending (feed! peer @pending chunk))))\n   184\t         (.on js/process.stdin \"end\" (fn [] (exit!))))\n   185\t\n   186\t       :default nil)))\n     1\t(ns dao.stream.slice-test\n     2\t  \"Phase 5 — the WebSocket slice, end to end, across two operating-system\n     3\t   processes on the JVM.\n     4\t\n     5\t   This namespace is process A.  It creates a ring buffer, serves it over two\n     6\t   independent WebSocket endpoints, and appends.  Process B is\n     7\t   `dao.stream.slice-peer`, spawned as a real child process; it obtains A's\n     8\t   descriptor as Transit JSON text on its command line — the bootstrap channel\n     9\t   is part of the test, not an assumption — attaches, appends outbound, and\n    10\t   reports what its own deposit medium received.\n    11\t\n    12\t   Nothing is shared between A and B but bytes on a pipe and bytes on a\n    13\t   socket.  That is what a same-process socket test cannot establish, and it\n    14\t   is why the plan requires two processes here.\n    15\t\n    16\t   The five facts of the plan's Phase 5 are one `deftest` each.  They share one\n    17\t   process A through a `:once` fixture, because fact 2 is precisely that the\n    18\t   served stream survives a connection's death: a per-test server would make\n    19\t   survival unfalsifiable.\"\n    20\t  (:require [clojure.java.io :as io]\n    21\t            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing use-fixtures]]\n    22\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    23\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\n    24\t            [dao.stream.serving :as serving]\n    25\t            [dao.stream.transit :as transit]\n    26\t            [dao.stream.ws :as ws]\n    27\t            [dao.stream.ws.jvm :as jvm]))\n    28\t\n    29\t\n    30\t;; =============================================================================\n    31\t;; Explicit composition data\n    32\t;; =============================================================================\n    33\t\n    34\t(def admission\n    35\t  {:retention :evict-oldest :capacity 256 :value-domain :portable-values})\n    36\t\n    37\t\n    38\t(def handoff-admission\n    39\t  {:retention :evict-oldest :capacity 1 :value-domain :host-values})\n    40\t\n    41\t\n    42\t(def served-identity\n    43\t  \"One logical stream, reachable two ways.  Fact 5 is that this value is what\n    44\t   both descriptors agree on while their reachability differs.\"\n    45\t  \"slice-served-stream\")\n    46\t\n    47\t\n    48\t(defn- buffer\n    49\t  ([] (buffer 256))\n    50\t  ([capacity]\n    51\t   (:dao.stream/handle (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n    52\t                                      ring/capacity-key capacity}))))\n    53\t\n    54\t\n    55\t(defn- newest\n    56\t  [handle]\n    57\t  (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor handle stream/anchor-newest)))\n    58\t\n    59\t\n    60\t(defn- drain\n    61\t  \"Every retained value on a medium, read from the oldest position.  Reads are\n    62\t   non-destructive, so this never disturbs the driver's own cursor.\"\n    63\t  [handle]\n    64\t  (loop [cursor (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor handle stream/anchor-oldest))\n    65\t         seen []]\n    66\t    (let [result (stream/next handle cursor)]\n    67\t      (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\n    68\t        (recur (:dao.stream/cursor result) (conj seen (:dao.stream/value result)))\n    69\t        seen))))\n    70\t\n    71\t\n    72\t(defn- table-descriptor\n    73\t  \"The served table's descriptor.  Its port is a placeholder because the bound\n    74\t   port is only known after listening; path lookup never consults the port, and\n    75\t   each test repairs reachability for its peer from the bound address.\"\n    76\t  [path]\n    77\t  {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/ws\n    78\t   :dao.stream/identity served-identity\n    79\t   :ws/host \"127.0.0.1\"\n    80\t   :ws/port 1\n    81\t   :ws/path path})\n    82\t\n    83\t\n    84\t;; =============================================================================\n    85\t;; Process A: one served ring buffer behind two endpoints\n    86\t;; =============================================================================\n    87\t\n    88\t(defn- make-endpoint-composition\n    89\t  \"Compose one serving endpoint over `source`, with `slot-count` capacity-one\n    90\t   acceptance-handoff slots.  Two slots would make fact 3 a race against the\n    91\t   driver's cadence rather than a test of attachment identity.\"\n    92\t  [source path slot-count]\n    93\t  (let [descriptor (table-descriptor path)\n    94\t        control (buffer)\n    95\t        slots (vec (repeatedly slot-count (fn [] {:offer (buffer 1) :ack (buffer 1)})))\n    96\t        endpoint (ws/make-endpoint\n    97\t                   {:served {path descriptor}\n    98\t                    :control {:dao.stream/handle control :dao.stream/surface #{:writer}}\n    99\t                    :control-admission admission\n   100\t                    :slots (mapv (fn [{:keys [offer ack]}]\n   101\t                                   {:offer {:dao.stream/handle offer\n   102\t                                            :dao.stream/surface #{:writer}}\n   103\t                                    :offer-admission handoff-admission\n   104\t                                    :ack {:dao.stream/handle ack\n   105\t                                          :dao.stream/surface #{:writer}}\n   106\t                                    :ack-admission handoff-admission\n   107\t                                    :ack-cursor (newest ack)})\n   108\t                                 slots)\n   109\t                    :expiry-ms nil})\n   110\t        media (atom {})\n   111\t        listener (atom nil)\n   112\t        port (atom nil)\n   113\t        lifecycle (atom [])\n   114\t        composition\n   115\t        (serving/make-serving\n   116\t          {:endpoint endpoint\n   117\t           :served {path {:descriptor descriptor :stream source}}\n   118\t           :control-reader control\n   119\t           :control-cursor (newest control)\n   120\t           :slots (mapv (fn [{:keys [offer ack]}]\n   121\t                          {:offer-reader offer\n   122\t                           :offer-cursor (newest offer)\n   123\t                           :ack-writer {:dao.stream/handle ack\n   124\t                                        :dao.stream/surface #{:writer}}})\n   125\t                        slots)\n   126\t           ;; Newest rather than the default oldest: these tests share one\n   127\t           ;; served stream, and a replay from oldest would let one fact's\n   128\t           ;; appends arrive at another fact's attachment.\n   129\t           :forward-anchor stream/anchor-newest\n   130\t           :forward-options {:batch-budget 16 :gap-policy :terminate}\n   131\t           :make-traffic (fn [offer-event]\n   132\t                           (let [traffic (buffer)]\n   133\t                             (swap! media assoc (:ws/attachment offer-event) traffic)\n   134\t                             {:traffic {:dao.stream/handle traffic\n   135\t                                        :dao.stream/surface #{:writer}}\n   136\t                              :admission admission\n   137\t                              :reader traffic\n   138\t                              :cursor (newest traffic)}))\n   139\t           ;; No `:inbound-step`: inbound payload stays ordinary traffic data\n   140\t           ;; on the per-attachment medium and is deliberately not interpreted\n   141\t           ;; into appends on the served stream.\n   142\t           :start-endpoint! (fn [ep]\n   143\t                              (let [result\n   144\t                                    (jvm/listen!\n   145\t                                      {:bind-host \"127.0.0.1\"\n   146\t                                       :bind-port 0\n   147\t                                       :accept! (fn [target socket now]\n   148\t                                                  (ws/accept-connection! ep target socket now))\n   149\t                                       :deposit! (fn [kind data]\n   150\t                                                   (swap! lifecycle conj [kind data])\n   151\t                                                   (when (= :bind-succeeded kind)\n   152\t                                                     (reset! port (:port data))))})]\n   153\t                                (reset! listener result)\n   154\t                                {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}))\n   155\t           :stop-endpoint! (fn [_]\n   156\t                             (jvm/stop-listening! @listener (fn [] nil)))})]\n   157\t    {:path path\n   158\t     :descriptor descriptor\n   159\t     :composition composition\n   160\t     :media media\n   161\t     :port port\n   162\t     :lifecycle lifecycle}))\n   163\t\n   164\t\n   165\t(def ^:private process-a (atom nil))\n   166\t\n   167\t\n   168\t(defn- start-process-a!\n   169\t  []\n   170\t  (let [source (buffer)\n   171\t        primary (make-endpoint-composition source \"/slice\" 4)\n   172\t        secondary (make-endpoint-composition source \"/slice-b\" 4)\n   173\t        running (atom true)]\n   174\t    (serving/start! (:composition primary))\n   175\t    (serving/start! (:composition secondary))\n   176\t    (let [driver (doto (Thread.\n   177\t                         (fn []\n   178\t                           (while @running\n   179\t                             (let [now (System/currentTimeMillis)]\n   180\t                               (serving/step! (:composition primary) now)\n   181\t                               (serving/step! (:composition secondary) now))\n   182\t                             (Thread/sleep 5)))\n   183\t                         \"slice-test-driver\")\n   184\t                   (.setDaemon true)\n   185\t                   (.start))]\n   186\t      {:source source\n   187\t       :primary primary\n   188\t       :secondary secondary\n   189\t       :running running\n   190\t       :driver driver})))\n   191\t\n   192\t\n   193\t(defn- stop-process-a!\n   194\t  [a]\n   195\t  (reset! (:running a) false)\n   196\t  (.join ^Thread (:driver a) 2000)\n   197\t  (serving/stop! (:composition (:primary a)))\n   198\t  (serving/stop! (:composition (:secondary a))))\n   199\t\n   200\t\n   201\t(defn- reachable\n   202\t  \"Repair a served descriptor's reachability from the bound port.  This is the\n   203\t   value that crosses to B as text, and the only thing B ever learns about A.\"\n   204\t  [endpoint]\n   205\t  (assoc (:descriptor endpoint) :ws/port @(:port endpoint)))\n   206\t\n   207\t\n   208\t;; =============================================================================\n   209\t;; Process B: a real child process, spoken to only over pipes\n   210\t;; =============================================================================\n   211\t\n   212\t(def ^:private peer-ready-ms 60000)\n   213\t(def ^:private reply-ms 15000)\n   214\t(def ^:private event-ms 15000)\n   215\t\n   216\t\n   217\t(defn- pump!\n   218\t  [reader on-line]\n   219\t  (doto (Thread.\n   220\t          (fn []\n   221\t            (try\n   222\t              (loop []\n   223\t                (when-let [line (.readLine ^java.io.BufferedReader reader)]\n   224\t                  (on-line line)\n   225\t                  (recur)))\n   226\t              (catch Exception _ nil))))\n   227\t    (.setDaemon true)\n   228\t    (.start)))\n   229\t\n   230\t\n   231\t(defn- start-peer!\n   232\t  \"Spawn process B on this process's own classpath.\n   233\t\n   234\t   Reusing the live classpath rather than shelling out to a fresh `clojure`\n   235\t   invocation keeps the child's startup to a JVM boot instead of a dependency\n   236\t   resolution, and guarantees B runs the same tree A does.\"\n   237\t  [descriptor]\n   238\t  (let [command [\"java\" \"-cp\" (System/getProperty \"java.class.path\")\n   239\t                 \"clojure.main\" \"-m\" \"dao.stream.slice-peer\"\n   240\t                 (transit/encode-descriptor descriptor)]\n   241\t        process (.start (ProcessBuilder. ^java.util.List command))\n   242\t        replies (atom [])\n   243\t        errors (atom [])\n   244\t        peer {:process process\n   245\t              :in (io/writer (.getOutputStream process))\n   246\t              :replies replies\n   247\t              :errors errors\n   248\t              :seen (atom [])}]\n   249\t    ;; Loading B's namespaces prints to B's stdout before the peer protocol\n   250\t    ;; starts, so a line that is not a Transit reply is noise rather than a\n   251\t    ;; protocol failure: recording it and carrying on keeps one banner from\n   252\t    ;; silently killing the reader and making every fact look unmet.\n   253\t    (pump! (io/reader (.getInputStream process))\n   254\t           (fn [line]\n   255\t             (let [reply (try (transit/decode line) (catch Exception _ nil))]\n   256\t               (if (:reply reply)\n   257\t                 (swap! replies conj reply)\n   258\t                 (swap! errors conj line)))))\n   259\t    ;; stderr must be drained too: an unread pipe fills and would block the\n   260\t    ;; child mid-report, which would look exactly like a failed assertion.\n   261\t    (pump! (io/reader (.getErrorStream process))\n   262\t           (fn [line] (swap! errors conj line)))\n   263\t    peer))\n   264\t\n   265\t\n   266\t(defn- stop-peer!\n   267\t  [peer]\n   268\t  (try (.destroy ^Process (:process peer)) (catch Exception _ nil)))\n   269\t\n   270\t\n   271\t(defn- take-reply!\n   272\t  \"Consume the first reply of `kind`, or nil at the deadline.\"\n   273\t  [peer kind timeout-ms]\n   274\t  (let [deadline (+ (System/currentTimeMillis) timeout-ms)]\n   275\t    (loop []\n   276\t      (let [index (first (keep-indexed (fn [i r] (when (= kind (:reply r)) i))\n   277\t                                       @(:replies peer)))]\n   278\t        (cond\n   279\t          index (let [reply (nth @(:replies peer) index)]\n   280\t                  (swap! (:replies peer)\n   281\t                         (fn [rs] (vec (concat (subvec rs 0 index) (subvec rs (inc index))))))\n   282\t                  reply)\n   283\t          (< deadline (System/currentTimeMillis)) nil\n   284\t          :else (do (Thread/sleep 5) (recur)))))))\n   285\t\n   286\t\n   287\t(defn- ask!\n   288\t  [peer command kind timeout-ms]\n   289\t  (let [writer ^java.io.Writer (:in peer)]\n   290\t    (.write writer (str (transit/encode command) \"\\n\"))\n   291\t    (.flush writer))\n   292\t  (take-reply! peer kind timeout-ms))\n   293\t\n   294\t\n   295\t(defn- poll-events!\n   296\t  \"Ask B for whatever its medium has accumulated since B last reported, and\n   297\t   remember it.  B advances only its own kept cursor; A never touches it.\"\n   298\t  [peer]\n   299\t  (swap! (:seen peer) into (:events (ask! peer {:cmd :events} :events reply-ms)))\n   300\t  @(:seen peer))\n   301\t\n   302\t\n   303\t(defn- await-event\n   304\t  [peer pred timeout-ms]\n   305\t  (let [deadline (+ (System/currentTimeMillis) timeout-ms)]\n   306\t    (loop []\n   307\t      (if-let [hit (first (filter pred (poll-events! peer)))]\n   308\t        hit\n   309\t        (when-not (< deadline (System/currentTimeMillis))\n   310\t          (Thread/sleep 20)\n   311\t          (recur))))))\n   312\t\n   313\t\n   314\t(defn- attach-peer!\n   315\t  \"Spawn B, wait for its bootstrap, attach, and wait for the opened event.\"\n   316\t  [descriptor]\n   317\t  (let [peer (start-peer! descriptor)\n   318\t        ready (take-reply! peer :ready peer-ready-ms)]\n   319\t    (is (some? ready)\n   320\t        (str \"process B never reported its bootstrap; its other output was \"\n   321\t             (pr-str @(:errors peer))))\n   322\t    (is (= descriptor (:descriptor ready))\n   323\t        \"the descriptor B decoded from text differs from the one A encoded\")\n   324\t    (let [attach (ask! peer {:cmd :attach} :attach reply-ms)]\n   325\t      (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:outcome attach)))\n   326\t      (is (some? (await-event peer #(= :ws/opened (:ws/event %)) event-ms))\n   327\t          \"the attachment never opened\")\n   328\t      (assoc peer :attachment (:attachment attach)))))\n   329\t\n   330\t\n   331\t(defn- server-attachment\n   332\t  \"Correlate B to the server-side session it joined by the token it appended.\n   333\t   The two sides mint their own attachment identities, so nothing but a\n   334\t   payload can connect them — which is itself worth asserting.\"\n   335\t  [endpoint token]\n   336\t  (let [deadline (+ (System/currentTimeMillis) event-ms)]\n   337\t    (loop []\n   338\t      (let [hit (first (filter (fn [[_ medium]]\n   339\t                                 (some #(= token (:ws/value %)) (drain medium)))\n   340\t                               @(:media endpoint)))]\n   341\t        (cond\n   342\t          hit (first hit)\n   343\t          (< deadline (System/currentTimeMillis)) nil\n   344\t          :else (do (Thread/sleep 20) (recur)))))))\n   345\t\n   346\t\n   347\t;; =============================================================================\n   348\t;; Fixture\n   349\t;; =============================================================================\n   350\t\n   351\t(use-fixtures :once\n   352\t  (fn [run]\n   353\t    (reset! process-a (start-process-a!))\n   354\t    (try (run)\n   355\t         (finally\n   356\t           (stop-process-a! @process-a)\n   357\t           (reset! process-a nil)))))\n   358\t\n   359\t\n   360\t;; =============================================================================\n   361\t;; The five facts\n   362\t;; =============================================================================\n   363\t\n   364\t(deftest detachment-is-observable-on-both-sides\n   365\t  ;; Fact 1.\n   366\t  (let [{:keys [source primary]} @process-a\n   367\t        peer (attach-peer! (reachable primary))]\n   368\t    (try\n   369\t      (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:outcome (ask! peer {:cmd :append :value :slice/established}\n   370\t                                            :append reply-ms)))\n   371\t          \"an established attachment must accept an outbound append\")\n   372\t      (let [token [:slice/fact-1 (:attachment peer)]]\n   373\t        (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:outcome (ask! peer {:cmd :append :value token}\n   374\t                                              :append reply-ms))))\n   375\t        (let [attachment (server-attachment primary token)]\n   376\t          (is (some? attachment) \"A never received B's outbound payload\")\n   377\t\n   378\t          ;; Kill the connection from B's side.\n   379\t          (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:outcome (ask! peer {:cmd :close} :close reply-ms))))\n   380\t\n   381\t          (testing \"B's handle answers closed\"\n   382\t            (is (= :dao.stream/closed\n   383\t                   (:outcome (ask! peer {:cmd :append :value :after-close}\n   384\t                                   :append reply-ms))))\n   385\t            (is (some? (await-event peer #(= :ws/closed (:ws/event %)) event-ms))\n   386\t                \"B's own medium never received the terminal event\"))\n   387\t\n   388\t          (testing \"A's boundary deposits the departure\"\n   389\t            (let [deadline (+ (System/currentTimeMillis) event-ms)]\n   390\t              (loop []\n   391\t                (let [events (drain (get @(:media primary) attachment))]\n   392\t                  (when (and (not= :ws/closed (:ws/event (last events)))\n   393\t                             (< (System/currentTimeMillis) deadline))\n   394\t                    (Thread/sleep 20)\n   395\t                    (recur)))))\n   396\t            (is (= :ws/closed (:ws/event (last (drain (get @(:media primary) attachment)))))\n   397\t                \"A's per-attachment medium never deposited the departure\")\n   398\t            (is (not (contains? (:sessions (serving/state (:composition primary)))\n   399\t                                attachment))\n   400\t                \"the driver kept a session for a departed attachment\"))\n   401\t\n   402\t          (testing \"the served stream is untouched by a connection's death\"\n   403\t            (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome\n   404\t                                    (stream/append! source :slice/still-alive)))))))\n   405\t      (finally (stop-peer! peer)))))\n   406\t\n   407\t\n   408\t(deftest the-same-descriptor-rejoins-the-same-logical-stream\n   409\t  ;; Fact 2.  The peer from fact 1 is gone; this one attaches, is killed, and\n   410\t  ;; reattaches with the identical bootstrapped descriptor value.\n   411\t  (let [{:keys [source primary]} @process-a\n   412\t        peer (attach-peer! (reachable primary))]\n   413\t    (try\n   414\t      (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:outcome (ask! peer {:cmd :close} :close reply-ms))))\n   415\t      (is (some? (await-event peer #(= :ws/closed (:ws/event %)) event-ms)))\n   416\t      (let [again (ask! peer {:cmd :attach} :attach reply-ms)]\n   417\t        (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:outcome again))\n   418\t            \"reattachment with the same descriptor was refused\")\n   419\t        (is (not= (:attachment peer) (:attachment again))\n   420\t            \"a reattachment is a new attachment, not a resurrected one\")\n     1\t(ns dao.stream.slice-test\n     2\t  \"Phase 5 — the WebSocket slice, end to end, across two operating-system\n     3\t   processes on Node.\n     4\t\n     5\t   The JVM half of this phase is `test/dao/stream/slice_test.clj`, which\n     6\t   carries the same five facts against the same peer program.  The two files\n     7\t   share a namespace name and no code: one is invisible to the other's\n     8\t   compiler, and the plan's host matrix wants Node server plus Node client\n     9\t   proven as its own slice rather than inferred from the JVM run.\n    10\t\n    11\t   Process A is here.  Process B is `dao.stream.slice-peer`, compiled by\n    12\t   the `:slice-peer` shadow build to `target/slice-peer.js` and spawned as a\n    13\t   real child `node` process — see the `test:cljs` task in `bb.edn`, which\n    14\t   compiles that build before this one.  B receives A's descriptor as Transit\n    15\t   JSON text in `argv` and learns nothing else about A.\n    16\t\n    17\t   Node is single-threaded, so every wait here is a turn on the event loop:\n    18\t   the driver is an explicit `setInterval` the test owns, and each step of a\n    19\t   fact is a promise that polls.  Nothing in the transport schedules itself.\"\n    20\t  (:require [\"child_process\" :as child-process]\n    21\t            [cljs.test :refer [async deftest is testing]]\n    22\t            [clojure.string :as str]\n    23\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    24\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\n    25\t            [dao.stream.serving :as serving]\n    26\t            [dao.stream.transit :as transit]\n    27\t            [dao.stream.ws :as ws]\n    28\t            [dao.stream.ws.node :as node]))\n    29\t\n    30\t\n    31\t;; =============================================================================\n    32\t;; Explicit composition data\n    33\t;; =============================================================================\n    34\t\n    35\t(def admission\n    36\t  {:retention :evict-oldest :capacity 256 :value-domain :portable-values})\n    37\t\n    38\t\n    39\t(def handoff-admission\n    40\t  {:retention :evict-oldest :capacity 1 :value-domain :host-values})\n    41\t\n    42\t\n    43\t(def served-identity\n    44\t  \"One logical stream, reachable two ways.  Fact 5 is that this value is what\n    45\t   both descriptors agree on while their reachability differs.\"\n    46\t  \"slice-served-stream\")\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\t(def peer-script \"target/slice-peer.js\")\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\t(def bind-ms 5000)\n    53\t(def reply-ms 10000)\n    54\t(def event-ms 10000)\n    55\t\n    56\t\n    57\t(defn- buffer\n    58\t  ([] (buffer 256))\n    59\t  ([capacity]\n    60\t   (:dao.stream/handle (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n    61\t                                      ring/capacity-key capacity}))))\n    62\t\n    63\t\n    64\t(defn- newest\n    65\t  [handle]\n    66\t  (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor handle stream/anchor-newest)))\n    67\t\n    68\t\n    69\t(defn- drain\n    70\t  \"Every retained value on a medium, read from the oldest position.  Reads are\n    71\t   non-destructive, so this never disturbs the driver's own cursor.\"\n    72\t  [handle]\n    73\t  (loop [cursor (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor handle stream/anchor-oldest))\n    74\t         seen []]\n    75\t    (let [result (stream/next handle cursor)]\n    76\t      (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\n    77\t        (recur (:dao.stream/cursor result) (conj seen (:dao.stream/value result)))\n    78\t        seen))))\n    79\t\n    80\t\n    81\t(defn- table-descriptor\n    82\t  \"The served table's descriptor.  Its port is a placeholder because the bound\n    83\t   port is only known after listening; path lookup never consults the port, and\n    84\t   each test repairs reachability for its peer from the bound address.\"\n    85\t  [path]\n    86\t  {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/ws\n    87\t   :dao.stream/identity served-identity\n    88\t   :ws/host \"127.0.0.1\"\n    89\t   :ws/port 1\n    90\t   :ws/path path})\n    91\t\n    92\t\n    93\t;; =============================================================================\n    94\t;; Process A: one served ring buffer behind two endpoints\n    95\t;; =============================================================================\n    96\t\n    97\t(defn- make-endpoint-composition\n    98\t  \"Compose one serving endpoint over `source`, with `slot-count` capacity-one\n    99\t   acceptance-handoff slots.  One slot would make fact 3 a race against the\n   100\t   driver's cadence rather than a test of attachment identity.\"\n   101\t  [source path slot-count]\n   102\t  (let [descriptor (table-descriptor path)\n   103\t        control (buffer)\n   104\t        slots (vec (repeatedly slot-count (fn [] {:offer (buffer 1) :ack (buffer 1)})))\n   105\t        endpoint (ws/make-endpoint\n   106\t                   {:served {path descriptor}\n   107\t                    :control {:dao.stream/handle control :dao.stream/surface #{:writer}}\n   108\t                    :control-admission admission\n   109\t                    :slots (mapv (fn [{:keys [offer ack]}]\n   110\t                                   {:offer {:dao.stream/handle offer\n   111\t                                            :dao.stream/surface #{:writer}}\n   112\t                                    :offer-admission handoff-admission\n   113\t                                    :ack {:dao.stream/handle ack\n   114\t                                          :dao.stream/surface #{:writer}}\n   115\t                                    :ack-admission handoff-admission\n   116\t                                    :ack-cursor (newest ack)})\n   117\t                                 slots)\n   118\t                    :expiry-ms nil})\n   119\t        media (atom {})\n   120\t        listener (atom nil)\n   121\t        composition\n   122\t        (serving/make-serving\n   123\t          {:endpoint endpoint\n   124\t           :served {path {:descriptor descriptor :stream source}}\n   125\t           :control-reader control\n   126\t           :control-cursor (newest control)\n   127\t           :slots (mapv (fn [{:keys [offer ack]}]\n   128\t                          {:offer-reader offer\n   129\t                           :offer-cursor (newest offer)\n   130\t                           :ack-writer {:dao.stream/handle ack\n   131\t                                        :dao.stream/surface #{:writer}}})\n   132\t                        slots)\n   133\t           ;; Newest rather than the default oldest: an attachment observes\n   134\t           ;; what is appended after it joined, so one fact's appends cannot\n   135\t           ;; be replayed into another fact's attachment.\n   136\t           :forward-anchor stream/anchor-newest\n   137\t           :forward-options {:batch-budget 16 :gap-policy :terminate}\n   138\t           :make-traffic (fn [offer-event]\n   139\t                           (let [traffic (buffer)]\n   140\t                             (swap! media assoc (:ws/attachment offer-event) traffic)\n   141\t                             {:traffic {:dao.stream/handle traffic\n   142\t                                        :dao.stream/surface #{:writer}}\n   143\t                              :admission admission\n   144\t                              :reader traffic\n   145\t                              :cursor (newest traffic)}))\n   146\t           ;; No `:inbound-step`: inbound payload stays ordinary traffic data\n   147\t           ;; on the per-attachment medium and is deliberately not interpreted\n   148\t           ;; into appends on the served stream.\n   149\t           :start-endpoint! (fn [ep]\n   150\t                              (reset! listener (node/listen! ep {:host \"127.0.0.1\"\n   151\t                                                                 :port 0}))\n   152\t                              {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok})\n   153\t           :stop-endpoint! (fn [_]\n   154\t                             (node/stop-listening! @listener)\n   155\t                             {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok})})]\n   156\t    {:path path\n   157\t     :descriptor descriptor\n   158\t     :composition composition\n   159\t     :media media\n   160\t     :listener listener}))\n   161\t\n   162\t\n   163\t(defn- server-fixture\n   164\t  []\n   165\t  (let [source (buffer)]\n   166\t    {:source source\n   167\t     :primary (make-endpoint-composition source \"/slice\" 4)\n   168\t     :secondary (make-endpoint-composition source \"/slice-b\" 4)}))\n   169\t\n   170\t\n   171\t(defn- reachable\n   172\t  \"Repair a served descriptor's reachability from the bound port.  This is the\n   173\t   value that crosses to B as text, and the only thing B ever learns about A.\"\n   174\t  [endpoint]\n   175\t  (assoc (:descriptor endpoint) :ws/port (node/listener-port @(:listener endpoint))))\n   176\t\n   177\t\n   178\t;; =============================================================================\n   179\t;; Waiting, as promises over the event loop\n   180\t;; =============================================================================\n   181\t\n   182\t(defn- poll-until\n   183\t  \"Resolve with the first truthy value `pred` returns, or reject at the\n   184\t   deadline.  Polling is the only honest wait here: no operation blocks, and\n   185\t   nothing notifies.\"\n   186\t  [pred timeout-ms message]\n   187\t  (js/Promise.\n   188\t    (fn [resolve reject]\n   189\t      (let [deadline (+ (js/Date.now) timeout-ms)]\n   190\t        (letfn [(tick []\n   191\t                  (let [value (try (pred) (catch :default _ nil))]\n   192\t                    (cond\n   193\t                      value (resolve value)\n   194\t                      (< deadline (js/Date.now)) (reject (js/Error. message))\n   195\t                      :else (js/setTimeout tick 10))))]\n   196\t          (tick))))))\n   197\t\n   198\t\n   199\t;; =============================================================================\n   200\t;; Process B: a real child process, spoken to only over pipes\n   201\t;; =============================================================================\n   202\t\n   203\t(defn- line-reader\n   204\t  \"Collect whole newline-terminated lines out of a Node stream's chunks.\"\n   205\t  [readable on-line]\n   206\t  (let [pending (atom \"\")]\n   207\t    (.setEncoding ^js readable \"utf8\")\n   208\t    (.on ^js readable \"data\"\n   209\t         (fn [chunk]\n   210\t           (let [parts (str/split (str @pending chunk) #\"\\n\" -1)]\n   211\t             (reset! pending (last parts))\n   212\t             (doseq [line (butlast parts)\n   213\t                     :when (not (str/blank? line))]\n   214\t               (on-line line)))))))\n   215\t\n   216\t\n   217\t(defn- start-peer!\n   218\t  [descriptor]\n   219\t  (let [process (.spawn child-process \"node\"\n   220\t                        #js [peer-script (transit/encode-descriptor descriptor)]\n   221\t                        #js {:stdio #js [\"pipe\" \"pipe\" \"pipe\"]})\n   222\t        replies (atom [])\n   223\t        errors (atom [])]\n   224\t    ;; Loading B's namespaces may print to B's stdout before the peer protocol\n   225\t    ;; starts, so a line that is not a Transit reply is noise rather than a\n   226\t    ;; protocol failure: recording it and carrying on keeps one banner from\n   227\t    ;; silently stopping the reader.\n   228\t    (line-reader (.-stdout process)\n   229\t                 (fn [line]\n   230\t                   (let [reply (try (transit/decode line) (catch :default _ nil))]\n   231\t                     (if (:reply reply)\n   232\t                       (swap! replies conj reply)\n   233\t                       (swap! errors conj line)))))\n   234\t    (line-reader (.-stderr process) (fn [line] (swap! errors conj line)))\n   235\t    {:process process :replies replies :errors errors :seen (atom [])}))\n   236\t\n   237\t\n   238\t(defn- stop-peer!\n   239\t  [peer]\n   240\t  (try (.kill ^js (:process peer)) (catch :default _ nil)))\n   241\t\n   242\t\n   243\t(defn- take-reply!\n   244\t  \"Consume the first reply of `kind`.\"\n   245\t  [peer kind]\n   246\t  (poll-until\n   247\t    (fn []\n   248\t      (when-let [index (first (keep-indexed (fn [i r] (when (= kind (:reply r)) i))\n   249\t                                            @(:replies peer)))]\n   250\t        (let [reply (nth @(:replies peer) index)]\n   251\t          (swap! (:replies peer)\n   252\t                 (fn [rs] (vec (concat (subvec rs 0 index) (subvec rs (inc index))))))\n   253\t          reply)))\n   254\t    reply-ms\n   255\t    (str \"process B never replied \" kind \"; its other output was \"\n   256\t         (pr-str @(:errors peer)))))\n   257\t\n   258\t\n   259\t(defn- ask!\n   260\t  [peer command kind]\n   261\t  (.write ^js (.-stdin ^js (:process peer)) (str (transit/encode command) \"\\n\"))\n   262\t  (take-reply! peer kind))\n   263\t\n   264\t\n   265\t(defn- poll-events!\n   266\t  \"Ask B for whatever its medium has accumulated since B last reported, and\n   267\t   remember it.  B advances only its own kept cursor; A never touches it.\"\n   268\t  [peer]\n   269\t  (.then (ask! peer {:cmd :events} :events)\n   270\t         (fn [reply]\n   271\t           (swap! (:seen peer) into (:events reply))\n   272\t           @(:seen peer))))\n   273\t\n   274\t\n   275\t(defn- await-event\n   276\t  [peer pred message]\n   277\t  (let [deadline (+ (js/Date.now) event-ms)]\n   278\t    (js/Promise.\n   279\t      (fn [resolve reject]\n   280\t        (letfn [(tick []\n   281\t                  (.then (poll-events! peer)\n   282\t                         (fn [seen]\n   283\t                           (if-let [hit (first (filter pred seen))]\n   284\t                             (resolve hit)\n   285\t                             (if (< deadline (js/Date.now))\n   286\t                               (reject (js/Error. message))\n   287\t                               (js/setTimeout tick 20))))\n   288\t                         reject))]\n   289\t          (tick))))))\n   290\t\n   291\t\n   292\t(defn- attach-peer!\n   293\t  \"Spawn B, wait for its bootstrap, attach, and wait for the opened event.\"\n   294\t  [peers descriptor]\n   295\t  (let [peer (start-peer! descriptor)]\n   296\t    (swap! peers conj peer)\n   297\t    (-> (take-reply! peer :ready)\n   298\t        (.then (fn [ready]\n   299\t                 (is (= descriptor (:descriptor ready))\n   300\t                     \"the descriptor B decoded from text differs from the one A encoded\")\n   301\t                 (ask! peer {:cmd :attach} :attach)))\n   302\t        (.then (fn [attach]\n   303\t                 (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:outcome attach)))\n   304\t                 (.then (await-event peer #(= :ws/opened (:ws/event %))\n   305\t                                     \"the attachment never opened\")\n   306\t                        (fn [_] (assoc peer :attachment (:attachment attach)))))))))\n   307\t\n   308\t\n   309\t(defn- server-attachment\n   310\t  \"Correlate B to the server-side session it joined by the token it appended.\n   311\t   The two sides mint their own attachment identities, so nothing but a\n   312\t   payload can connect them — which is itself worth asserting.\"\n   313\t  [endpoint token]\n   314\t  (poll-until\n   315\t    (fn []\n   316\t      (first (first (filter (fn [[_ medium]]\n   317\t                              (some #(= token (:ws/value %)) (drain medium)))\n   318\t                            @(:media endpoint)))))\n   319\t    event-ms\n   320\t    \"A never received B's outbound payload\"))\n   321\t\n   322\t\n   323\t(defn- run-slice\n   324\t  \"Start process A, run one fact, then tear everything down exactly once.\"\n   325\t  [done body]\n   326\t  (let [fixture (server-fixture)\n   327\t        peers (atom [])]\n   328\t    (serving/start! (:composition (:primary fixture)))\n   329\t    (serving/start! (:composition (:secondary fixture)))\n   330\t    (let [ticker (js/setInterval\n   331\t                   (fn []\n   332\t                     (let [now (js/Date.now)]\n   333\t                       (serving/step! (:composition (:primary fixture)) now)\n   334\t                       (serving/step! (:composition (:secondary fixture)) now)))\n   335\t                   5)\n   336\t          teardown (fn []\n   337\t                     (js/clearInterval ticker)\n   338\t                     (doseq [peer @peers] (stop-peer! peer))\n   339\t                     (serving/stop! (:composition (:primary fixture)))\n   340\t                     (serving/stop! (:composition (:secondary fixture))))]\n   341\t      (-> (poll-until #(and (node/listener-port @(:listener (:primary fixture)))\n   342\t                            (node/listener-port @(:listener (:secondary fixture))))\n   343\t                      bind-ms\n   344\t                      \"the listeners never reported bound ports\")\n   345\t          (.then (fn [_] (body fixture peers)))\n   346\t          (.then (fn [_] nil)\n   347\t                 (fn [error] (is false (str \"slice failure: \" (.-message ^js error)))))\n   348\t          (.then (fn [_] (teardown) (done)))))))\n   349\t\n   350\t\n   351\t;; =============================================================================\n   352\t;; The five facts\n   353\t;; =============================================================================\n   354\t\n   355\t(deftest detachment-is-observable-on-both-sides\n   356\t  ;; Fact 1.\n   357\t  (async done\n   358\t    (run-slice\n   359\t      done\n   360\t      (fn [{:keys [source primary]} peers]\n   361\t        (let [me (atom nil)\n   362\t              token (atom nil)\n   363\t              attachment (atom nil)]\n   364\t          (-> (attach-peer! peers (reachable primary))\n   365\t              (.then (fn [peer]\n   366\t                       (reset! me peer)\n   367\t                       (reset! token [:slice/fact-1 (:attachment peer)])\n   368\t                       (ask! peer {:cmd :append :value :slice/established} :append)))\n   369\t              (.then (fn [reply]\n   370\t                       (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:outcome reply))\n   371\t                           \"an established attachment must accept an outbound append\")\n   372\t                       (ask! @me {:cmd :append :value @token} :append)))\n   373\t              (.then (fn [reply]\n   374\t                       (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:outcome reply)))\n   375\t                       (server-attachment primary @token)))\n   376\t              (.then (fn [server-side]\n   377\t                       (reset! attachment server-side)\n   378\t                       ;; Kill the connection from B's side.\n   379\t                       (ask! @me {:cmd :close} :close)))\n   380\t              (.then (fn [reply]\n   381\t                       (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:outcome reply)))\n   382\t                       (ask! @me {:cmd :append :value :after-close} :append)))\n   383\t              (.then (fn [reply]\n   384\t                       (testing \"B's handle answers closed\"\n   385\t                         (is (= :dao.stream/closed (:outcome reply))))\n   386\t                       (await-event @me #(= :ws/closed (:ws/event %))\n   387\t                                    \"B's own medium never received the terminal event\")))\n   388\t              (.then (fn [_]\n   389\t                       (poll-until\n   390\t                         #(= :ws/closed (:ws/event (last (drain (get @(:media primary)\n   391\t                                                                    @attachment)))))\n   392\t                         event-ms\n   393\t                         \"A's per-attachment medium never deposited the departure\")))\n   394\t              (.then (fn [_]\n   395\t                       (testing \"A's boundary deposits the departure\"\n   396\t                         (is (not (contains? (:sessions (serving/state (:composition primary)))\n   397\t                                             @attachment))\n   398\t                             \"the driver kept a session for a departed attachment\"))\n   399\t                       (testing \"the served stream is untouched by a connection's death\"\n   400\t                         (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome\n   401\t                                                 (stream/append! source :slice/still-alive)))))))))))))\n   402\t\n   403\t\n   404\t(deftest the-same-descriptor-rejoins-the-same-logical-stream\n   405\t  ;; Fact 2.\n   406\t  (async done\n   407\t    (run-slice\n   408\t      done\n   409\t      (fn [{:keys [source primary]} peers]\n   410\t        (let [me (atom nil)\n   411\t              first-attachment (atom nil)\n   412\t              again (atom nil)\n   413\t              token (atom nil)]\n   414\t          (-> (attach-peer! peers (reachable primary))\n   415\t              (.then (fn [peer]\n   416\t                       (reset! me peer)\n   417\t                       (reset! first-attachment (:attachment peer))\n   418\t                       (ask! peer {:cmd :close} :close)))\n   419\t              (.then (fn [reply]\n   420\t                       (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:outcome reply)))\n     1\t;; shadow-cljs configuration\n     2\t;; Source paths come from deps.edn (:paths plus the :cljs alias's\n     3\t;; :extra-paths); shadow ignores any :source-paths set here when :deps\n     4\t;; is used.\n     5\t{:deps {:aliases [:cljs]}\n     6\t\n     7\t :dev-http {9000 \"public\"}\n     8\t\n     9\t :builds {:demo {:target :browser\n    10\t                 :devtools {:use-document-protocol true}\n    11\t                 :modules {:main {:init-fn datomworld.demo/init}}}\n    12\t\n    13\t          :local {:target :browser\n    14\t                  :devtools {:use-document-protocol true}\n    15\t                  :closure-defines {datomworld.demo/WEBSOCKET_PORT 8090}\n    16\t                  :modules {:main {:init-fn datomworld.demo/init}}}\n    17\t\n    18\t          :test {:target :node-test\n    19\t                 :output-to \"target/node-tests.js\"\n    20\t                 :autorun true}\n    21\t\n    22\t          :bench {:target :node-script\n    23\t                  :main dao.stream-bench/-main\n    24\t                  :output-to \"target/bench.js\"}\n    25\t\n    26\t          :slice-peer {:target :node-script\n    27\t                       :main dao.stream.slice-peer/-main\n    28\t                       :output-to \"target/slice-peer.js\"}\n    29\t\n    30\t          :yin-repl {:target :node-script\n    31\t                     :main yin.repl/-main\n    32\t                     :output-to \"target/yin-repl.js\"}\n    33\t\n    34\t          :yin-repl {:target :node-script\n    35\t                        :main yin.repl/-main\n    36\t                        :output-to \"target/yin-repl.js\"}\n    37\t\n    38\t          :ws-client-demo {:target :node-script\n    39\t                           :main datomworld.ws-client-demo/-main\n    40\t                           :output-to \"target/ws-client-demo.js\"}\n    41\t\n    42\t          :telemetry-server\n    43\t          {:target     :node-script\n    44\t           :main       yin.vm.telemetry-server.node/-main\n    45\t           :output-to  \"target/telemetry-server.js\"}\n    46\t\n    47\t          :telemetry-viewer\n    48\t          {:target   :browser\n    49\t           :devtools {:use-document-protocol true}\n    50\t           :output-dir \"public/js/telemetry-viewer\"\n    51\t           :asset-path \"/js/telemetry-viewer\"\n    52\t           :closure-defines\n    53\t           {yin.vm.telemetry-viewer/REPL_PORT 8090\n    54\t            yin.vm.telemetry-viewer/TEL_PORT  8091}\n    55\t           :modules  {:main {:init-fn yin.vm.telemetry-viewer/init}}}}}\n     1\t{:tasks\n     2\t {test:clj {:doc \"Run JVM tests (via clj)\"\n     3\t            :task (shell \"clojure -M:test\")}\n     4\t  \n     5\t  test:cljs {:doc \"Run Node tests (via shadow-cljs with :cljs alias)\"\n     6\t             :task (shell \"clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile slice-peer test\")}\n     7\t  \n     8\t  test:cljd {:doc \"Run Dart tests (via clojure -M:cljd)\"\n     9\t             :task (shell \"clojure -M:cljd test\")}\n    10\t  \n    11\t  test {:doc \"Run all tests\"\n    12\t        :depends [test:clj test:cljs test:cljd]}}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/dao/stream/slice_test.clj | sed -n '200,520p'; nl -ba test/dao/stream/slice_test.clj | sed -n '520,820p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/dao/stream/slice_test.clj | sed -n '200,520p'; nl -ba test/dao/stream/slice_test.clj | sed -n '520,820p'\"","aggregated_output":"   200\t\n   201\t(defn- reachable\n   202\t  \"Repair a served descriptor's reachability from the bound port.  This is the\n   203\t   value that crosses to B as text, and the only thing B ever learns about A.\"\n   204\t  [endpoint]\n   205\t  (assoc (:descriptor endpoint) :ws/port @(:port endpoint)))\n   206\t\n   207\t\n   208\t;; =============================================================================\n   209\t;; Process B: a real child process, spoken to only over pipes\n   210\t;; =============================================================================\n   211\t\n   212\t(def ^:private peer-ready-ms 60000)\n   213\t(def ^:private reply-ms 15000)\n   214\t(def ^:private event-ms 15000)\n   215\t\n   216\t\n   217\t(defn- pump!\n   218\t  [reader on-line]\n   219\t  (doto (Thread.\n   220\t          (fn []\n   221\t            (try\n   222\t              (loop []\n   223\t                (when-let [line (.readLine ^java.io.BufferedReader reader)]\n   224\t                  (on-line line)\n   225\t                  (recur)))\n   226\t              (catch Exception _ nil))))\n   227\t    (.setDaemon true)\n   228\t    (.start)))\n   229\t\n   230\t\n   231\t(defn- start-peer!\n   232\t  \"Spawn process B on this process's own classpath.\n   233\t\n   234\t   Reusing the live classpath rather than shelling out to a fresh `clojure`\n   235\t   invocation keeps the child's startup to a JVM boot instead of a dependency\n   236\t   resolution, and guarantees B runs the same tree A does.\"\n   237\t  [descriptor]\n   238\t  (let [command [\"java\" \"-cp\" (System/getProperty \"java.class.path\")\n   239\t                 \"clojure.main\" \"-m\" \"dao.stream.slice-peer\"\n   240\t                 (transit/encode-descriptor descriptor)]\n   241\t        process (.start (ProcessBuilder. ^java.util.List command))\n   242\t        replies (atom [])\n   243\t        errors (atom [])\n   244\t        peer {:process process\n   245\t              :in (io/writer (.getOutputStream process))\n   246\t              :replies replies\n   247\t              :errors errors\n   248\t              :seen (atom [])}]\n   249\t    ;; Loading B's namespaces prints to B's stdout before the peer protocol\n   250\t    ;; starts, so a line that is not a Transit reply is noise rather than a\n   251\t    ;; protocol failure: recording it and carrying on keeps one banner from\n   252\t    ;; silently killing the reader and making every fact look unmet.\n   253\t    (pump! (io/reader (.getInputStream process))\n   254\t           (fn [line]\n   255\t             (let [reply (try (transit/decode line) (catch Exception _ nil))]\n   256\t               (if (:reply reply)\n   257\t                 (swap! replies conj reply)\n   258\t                 (swap! errors conj line)))))\n   259\t    ;; stderr must be drained too: an unread pipe fills and would block the\n   260\t    ;; child mid-report, which would look exactly like a failed assertion.\n   261\t    (pump! (io/reader (.getErrorStream process))\n   262\t           (fn [line] (swap! errors conj line)))\n   263\t    peer))\n   264\t\n   265\t\n   266\t(defn- stop-peer!\n   267\t  [peer]\n   268\t  (try (.destroy ^Process (:process peer)) (catch Exception _ nil)))\n   269\t\n   270\t\n   271\t(defn- take-reply!\n   272\t  \"Consume the first reply of `kind`, or nil at the deadline.\"\n   273\t  [peer kind timeout-ms]\n   274\t  (let [deadline (+ (System/currentTimeMillis) timeout-ms)]\n   275\t    (loop []\n   276\t      (let [index (first (keep-indexed (fn [i r] (when (= kind (:reply r)) i))\n   277\t                                       @(:replies peer)))]\n   278\t        (cond\n   279\t          index (let [reply (nth @(:replies peer) index)]\n   280\t                  (swap! (:replies peer)\n   281\t                         (fn [rs] (vec (concat (subvec rs 0 index) (subvec rs (inc index))))))\n   282\t                  reply)\n   283\t          (< deadline (System/currentTimeMillis)) nil\n   284\t          :else (do (Thread/sleep 5) (recur)))))))\n   285\t\n   286\t\n   287\t(defn- ask!\n   288\t  [peer command kind timeout-ms]\n   289\t  (let [writer ^java.io.Writer (:in peer)]\n   290\t    (.write writer (str (transit/encode command) \"\\n\"))\n   291\t    (.flush writer))\n   292\t  (take-reply! peer kind timeout-ms))\n   293\t\n   294\t\n   295\t(defn- poll-events!\n   296\t  \"Ask B for whatever its medium has accumulated since B last reported, and\n   297\t   remember it.  B advances only its own kept cursor; A never touches it.\"\n   298\t  [peer]\n   299\t  (swap! (:seen peer) into (:events (ask! peer {:cmd :events} :events reply-ms)))\n   300\t  @(:seen peer))\n   301\t\n   302\t\n   303\t(defn- await-event\n   304\t  [peer pred timeout-ms]\n   305\t  (let [deadline (+ (System/currentTimeMillis) timeout-ms)]\n   306\t    (loop []\n   307\t      (if-let [hit (first (filter pred (poll-events! peer)))]\n   308\t        hit\n   309\t        (when-not (< deadline (System/currentTimeMillis))\n   310\t          (Thread/sleep 20)\n   311\t          (recur))))))\n   312\t\n   313\t\n   314\t(defn- attach-peer!\n   315\t  \"Spawn B, wait for its bootstrap, attach, and wait for the opened event.\"\n   316\t  [descriptor]\n   317\t  (let [peer (start-peer! descriptor)\n   318\t        ready (take-reply! peer :ready peer-ready-ms)]\n   319\t    (is (some? ready)\n   320\t        (str \"process B never reported its bootstrap; its other output was \"\n   321\t             (pr-str @(:errors peer))))\n   322\t    (is (= descriptor (:descriptor ready))\n   323\t        \"the descriptor B decoded from text differs from the one A encoded\")\n   324\t    (let [attach (ask! peer {:cmd :attach} :attach reply-ms)]\n   325\t      (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:outcome attach)))\n   326\t      (is (some? (await-event peer #(= :ws/opened (:ws/event %)) event-ms))\n   327\t          \"the attachment never opened\")\n   328\t      (assoc peer :attachment (:attachment attach)))))\n   329\t\n   330\t\n   331\t(defn- server-attachment\n   332\t  \"Correlate B to the server-side session it joined by the token it appended.\n   333\t   The two sides mint their own attachment identities, so nothing but a\n   334\t   payload can connect them — which is itself worth asserting.\"\n   335\t  [endpoint token]\n   336\t  (let [deadline (+ (System/currentTimeMillis) event-ms)]\n   337\t    (loop []\n   338\t      (let [hit (first (filter (fn [[_ medium]]\n   339\t                                 (some #(= token (:ws/value %)) (drain medium)))\n   340\t                               @(:media endpoint)))]\n   341\t        (cond\n   342\t          hit (first hit)\n   343\t          (< deadline (System/currentTimeMillis)) nil\n   344\t          :else (do (Thread/sleep 20) (recur)))))))\n   345\t\n   346\t\n   347\t;; =============================================================================\n   348\t;; Fixture\n   349\t;; =============================================================================\n   350\t\n   351\t(use-fixtures :once\n   352\t  (fn [run]\n   353\t    (reset! process-a (start-process-a!))\n   354\t    (try (run)\n   355\t         (finally\n   356\t           (stop-process-a! @process-a)\n   357\t           (reset! process-a nil)))))\n   358\t\n   359\t\n   360\t;; =============================================================================\n   361\t;; The five facts\n   362\t;; =============================================================================\n   363\t\n   364\t(deftest detachment-is-observable-on-both-sides\n   365\t  ;; Fact 1.\n   366\t  (let [{:keys [source primary]} @process-a\n   367\t        peer (attach-peer! (reachable primary))]\n   368\t    (try\n   369\t      (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:outcome (ask! peer {:cmd :append :value :slice/established}\n   370\t                                            :append reply-ms)))\n   371\t          \"an established attachment must accept an outbound append\")\n   372\t      (let [token [:slice/fact-1 (:attachment peer)]]\n   373\t        (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:outcome (ask! peer {:cmd :append :value token}\n   374\t                                              :append reply-ms))))\n   375\t        (let [attachment (server-attachment primary token)]\n   376\t          (is (some? attachment) \"A never received B's outbound payload\")\n   377\t\n   378\t          ;; Kill the connection from B's side.\n   379\t          (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:outcome (ask! peer {:cmd :close} :close reply-ms))))\n   380\t\n   381\t          (testing \"B's handle answers closed\"\n   382\t            (is (= :dao.stream/closed\n   383\t                   (:outcome (ask! peer {:cmd :append :value :after-close}\n   384\t                                   :append reply-ms))))\n   385\t            (is (some? (await-event peer #(= :ws/closed (:ws/event %)) event-ms))\n   386\t                \"B's own medium never received the terminal event\"))\n   387\t\n   388\t          (testing \"A's boundary deposits the departure\"\n   389\t            (let [deadline (+ (System/currentTimeMillis) event-ms)]\n   390\t              (loop []\n   391\t                (let [events (drain (get @(:media primary) attachment))]\n   392\t                  (when (and (not= :ws/closed (:ws/event (last events)))\n   393\t                             (< (System/currentTimeMillis) deadline))\n   394\t                    (Thread/sleep 20)\n   395\t                    (recur)))))\n   396\t            (is (= :ws/closed (:ws/event (last (drain (get @(:media primary) attachment)))))\n   397\t                \"A's per-attachment medium never deposited the departure\")\n   398\t            (is (not (contains? (:sessions (serving/state (:composition primary)))\n   399\t                                attachment))\n   400\t                \"the driver kept a session for a departed attachment\"))\n   401\t\n   402\t          (testing \"the served stream is untouched by a connection's death\"\n   403\t            (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome\n   404\t                                    (stream/append! source :slice/still-alive)))))))\n   405\t      (finally (stop-peer! peer)))))\n   406\t\n   407\t\n   408\t(deftest the-same-descriptor-rejoins-the-same-logical-stream\n   409\t  ;; Fact 2.  The peer from fact 1 is gone; this one attaches, is killed, and\n   410\t  ;; reattaches with the identical bootstrapped descriptor value.\n   411\t  (let [{:keys [source primary]} @process-a\n   412\t        peer (attach-peer! (reachable primary))]\n   413\t    (try\n   414\t      (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:outcome (ask! peer {:cmd :close} :close reply-ms))))\n   415\t      (is (some? (await-event peer #(= :ws/closed (:ws/event %)) event-ms)))\n   416\t      (let [again (ask! peer {:cmd :attach} :attach reply-ms)]\n   417\t        (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:outcome again))\n   418\t            \"reattachment with the same descriptor was refused\")\n   419\t        (is (not= (:attachment peer) (:attachment again))\n   420\t            \"a reattachment is a new attachment, not a resurrected one\")\n   421\t        (is (some? (await-event peer (fn [event]\n   422\t                                       (and (= :ws/opened (:ws/event event))\n   423\t                                            (= (:attachment again) (:ws/attachment event))))\n   424\t                                event-ms)))\n   425\t        (let [token [:slice/fact-2 (:attachment again)]]\n   426\t          ;; A appends to the surviving logical stream; the rejoined\n   427\t          ;; attachment receives it, which is what \"same logical stream\" means\n   428\t          ;; operationally.\n   429\t          (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! source token))))\n   430\t          (is (some? (await-event peer #(= token (:ws/value %)) event-ms))\n   431\t              \"the rejoined attachment received nothing from the served stream\")))\n   432\t      (finally (stop-peer! peer)))))\n   433\t\n   434\t\n   435\t(deftest simultaneous-attachments-carry-distinct-attachment-identity\n   436\t  ;; Fact 3.  Two whole processes, so nothing but the wire could make their\n   437\t  ;; identities agree by accident.\n   438\t  (let [{:keys [source primary]} @process-a\n   439\t        descriptor (reachable primary)\n   440\t        peer-1 (attach-peer! descriptor)\n   441\t        peer-2 (attach-peer! descriptor)]\n   442\t    (try\n   443\t      (is (string? (:attachment peer-1)))\n   444\t      (is (string? (:attachment peer-2)))\n   445\t      (is (not= (:attachment peer-1) (:attachment peer-2))\n   446\t          \"two simultaneous attachments shared one attachment identity\")\n   447\t\n   448\t      (let [token-1 [:slice/fact-3 (:attachment peer-1)]\n   449\t            token-2 [:slice/fact-3 (:attachment peer-2)]]\n   450\t        (ask! peer-1 {:cmd :append :value token-1} :append reply-ms)\n   451\t        (ask! peer-2 {:cmd :append :value token-2} :append reply-ms)\n   452\t        (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! source :slice/fanout))))\n   453\t        (await-event peer-1 #(= :slice/fanout (:ws/value %)) event-ms)\n   454\t        (await-event peer-2 #(= :slice/fanout (:ws/value %)) event-ms)\n   455\t\n   456\t        (testing \"every event on a client medium carries that client's identity\"\n   457\t          (doseq [peer [peer-1 peer-2]]\n   458\t            (let [events (poll-events! peer)]\n   459\t              (is (seq events))\n   460\t              (is (every? #(= (:attachment peer) (:ws/attachment %)) events)\n   461\t                  \"an event on B's medium was attributed to another attachment\"))))\n   462\t\n   463\t        (testing \"every event on a server medium carries that session's identity\"\n   464\t          (let [a-1 (server-attachment primary token-1)\n   465\t                a-2 (server-attachment primary token-2)]\n   466\t            (is (some? a-1))\n   467\t            (is (some? a-2))\n   468\t            (is (not= a-1 a-2)\n   469\t                \"two connections were folded into one server-side attachment\")\n   470\t            (doseq [attachment [a-1 a-2]]\n   471\t              (let [events (drain (get @(:media primary) attachment))]\n   472\t                (is (seq events))\n   473\t                ;; Payload, resolution, and lifecycle alike.\n   474\t                (is (every? #(= attachment (:ws/attachment %)) events)))))))\n   475\t      (finally\n   476\t        (stop-peer! peer-1)\n   477\t        (stop-peer! peer-2)))))\n   478\t\n   479\t\n   480\t(deftest the-deposit-medium-outlives-the-socket\n   481\t  ;; Fact 4.  The cursor is B's, on B's medium; it is never handed to\n   482\t  ;; `attach!` and never used through the WebSocket handle.\n   483\t  (let [{:keys [source primary]} @process-a\n   484\t        peer (attach-peer! (reachable primary))]\n   485\t    (try\n   486\t      (is (= #{:writer :closable} (:value (ask! peer {:cmd :surfaces} :surfaces reply-ms)))\n   487\t          \"the ws handle must have no reader surface for this fact to mean anything\")\n   488\t\n   489\t      (let [token [:slice/fact-4 (:attachment peer)]]\n   490\t        (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! source token))))\n   491\t        (is (some? (await-event peer #(= token (:ws/value %)) event-ms))))\n   492\t\n   493\t      ;; The socket dies.  B's medium and B's position on it do not.\n   494\t      (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:outcome (ask! peer {:cmd :close} :close reply-ms))))\n   495\t      (is (some? (await-event peer #(= :ws/closed (:ws/event %)) event-ms))\n   496\t          \"the kept cursor did not resume across the socket's death\")\n   497\t\n   498\t      (testing \"the cursor resumed rather than restarted\"\n   499\t        ;; Every event B has reported came from one uninterrupted walk of one\n   500\t        ;; cursor: an opened, a payload, and exactly one terminal event, in\n   501\t        ;; order and without repetition.\n   502\t        (let [events @(:seen peer)]\n   503\t          (is (= [:ws/opened :ws/payload :ws/closed] (mapv :ws/event events)))\n   504\t          (is (apply distinct? events))))\n   505\t      (finally (stop-peer! peer)))))\n   506\t\n   507\t\n   508\t(deftest two-endpoints-differ-in-reachability-and-agree-on-identity\n   509\t  ;; Fact 5.\n   510\t  (let [{:keys [source primary secondary]} @process-a\n   511\t        d-1 (reachable primary)\n   512\t        d-2 (reachable secondary)]\n   513\t    (is (not= d-1 d-2) \"two endpoints produced the same descriptor\")\n   514\t    (is (not= (select-keys d-1 [:ws/host :ws/port :ws/path])\n   515\t              (select-keys d-2 [:ws/host :ws/port :ws/path]))\n   516\t        \"the two endpoints are not separately reachable\")\n   517\t    (is (= (:dao.stream/identity d-1) (:dao.stream/identity d-2))\n   518\t        \"one logical stream served twice must carry one identity\")\n   519\t\n   520\t    (let [peer-1 (attach-peer! d-1)\n   520\t    (let [peer-1 (attach-peer! d-1)\n   521\t          peer-2 (attach-peer! d-2)]\n   522\t      (try\n   523\t        (testing \"each handle projects its own reachability and the shared identity\"\n   524\t          (let [h-1 (ask! peer-1 {:cmd :handle-descriptor} :handle-descriptor reply-ms)\n   525\t                h-2 (ask! peer-2 {:cmd :handle-descriptor} :handle-descriptor reply-ms)]\n   526\t            (is (not= (:descriptor h-1) (:descriptor h-2)))\n   527\t            (is (= (:identity h-1) (:identity h-2)))\n   528\t            (is (= served-identity (:identity h-1)))))\n   529\t\n   530\t        (testing \"cursors compare identity, never a descriptor\"\n   531\t          ;; One cursor on the served stream is valid for the logical stream\n   532\t          ;; both endpoints serve; neither descriptor participates.\n   533\t          (let [minted (stream/cursor source stream/anchor-newest)]\n   534\t            (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome minted)))\n   535\t            (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! source :slice/both))))\n   536\t            (is (= :slice/both (:dao.stream/value\n   537\t                                 (stream/next source (:dao.stream/cursor minted)))))))\n   538\t\n   539\t        (testing \"both endpoints serve the same logical stream\"\n   540\t          (is (some? (await-event peer-1 #(= :slice/both (:ws/value %)) event-ms)))\n   541\t          (is (some? (await-event peer-2 #(= :slice/both (:ws/value %)) event-ms))))\n   542\t        (finally\n   543\t          (stop-peer! peer-1)\n   544\t          (stop-peer! peer-2))))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/dao/stream/slice_test.cljs | sed -n '1,220p'; nl -ba test/dao/stream/slice_test.cljs | sed -n '220,560p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/dao/stream/slice_test.cljs | sed -n '1,220p'; nl -ba test/dao/stream/slice_test.cljs | sed -n '220,560p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.stream.slice-test\n     2\t  \"Phase 5 — the WebSocket slice, end to end, across two operating-system\n     3\t   processes on Node.\n     4\t\n     5\t   The JVM half of this phase is `test/dao/stream/slice_test.clj`, which\n     6\t   carries the same five facts against the same peer program.  The two files\n     7\t   share a namespace name and no code: one is invisible to the other's\n     8\t   compiler, and the plan's host matrix wants Node server plus Node client\n     9\t   proven as its own slice rather than inferred from the JVM run.\n    10\t\n    11\t   Process A is here.  Process B is `dao.stream.slice-peer`, compiled by\n    12\t   the `:slice-peer` shadow build to `target/slice-peer.js` and spawned as a\n    13\t   real child `node` process — see the `test:cljs` task in `bb.edn`, which\n    14\t   compiles that build before this one.  B receives A's descriptor as Transit\n    15\t   JSON text in `argv` and learns nothing else about A.\n    16\t\n    17\t   Node is single-threaded, so every wait here is a turn on the event loop:\n    18\t   the driver is an explicit `setInterval` the test owns, and each step of a\n    19\t   fact is a promise that polls.  Nothing in the transport schedules itself.\"\n    20\t  (:require [\"child_process\" :as child-process]\n    21\t            [cljs.test :refer [async deftest is testing]]\n    22\t            [clojure.string :as str]\n    23\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    24\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\n    25\t            [dao.stream.serving :as serving]\n    26\t            [dao.stream.transit :as transit]\n    27\t            [dao.stream.ws :as ws]\n    28\t            [dao.stream.ws.node :as node]))\n    29\t\n    30\t\n    31\t;; =============================================================================\n    32\t;; Explicit composition data\n    33\t;; =============================================================================\n    34\t\n    35\t(def admission\n    36\t  {:retention :evict-oldest :capacity 256 :value-domain :portable-values})\n    37\t\n    38\t\n    39\t(def handoff-admission\n    40\t  {:retention :evict-oldest :capacity 1 :value-domain :host-values})\n    41\t\n    42\t\n    43\t(def served-identity\n    44\t  \"One logical stream, reachable two ways.  Fact 5 is that this value is what\n    45\t   both descriptors agree on while their reachability differs.\"\n    46\t  \"slice-served-stream\")\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\t(def peer-script \"target/slice-peer.js\")\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\t(def bind-ms 5000)\n    53\t(def reply-ms 10000)\n    54\t(def event-ms 10000)\n    55\t\n    56\t\n    57\t(defn- buffer\n    58\t  ([] (buffer 256))\n    59\t  ([capacity]\n    60\t   (:dao.stream/handle (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n    61\t                                      ring/capacity-key capacity}))))\n    62\t\n    63\t\n    64\t(defn- newest\n    65\t  [handle]\n    66\t  (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor handle stream/anchor-newest)))\n    67\t\n    68\t\n    69\t(defn- drain\n    70\t  \"Every retained value on a medium, read from the oldest position.  Reads are\n    71\t   non-destructive, so this never disturbs the driver's own cursor.\"\n    72\t  [handle]\n    73\t  (loop [cursor (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor handle stream/anchor-oldest))\n    74\t         seen []]\n    75\t    (let [result (stream/next handle cursor)]\n    76\t      (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\n    77\t        (recur (:dao.stream/cursor result) (conj seen (:dao.stream/value result)))\n    78\t        seen))))\n    79\t\n    80\t\n    81\t(defn- table-descriptor\n    82\t  \"The served table's descriptor.  Its port is a placeholder because the bound\n    83\t   port is only known after listening; path lookup never consults the port, and\n    84\t   each test repairs reachability for its peer from the bound address.\"\n    85\t  [path]\n    86\t  {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/ws\n    87\t   :dao.stream/identity served-identity\n    88\t   :ws/host \"127.0.0.1\"\n    89\t   :ws/port 1\n    90\t   :ws/path path})\n    91\t\n    92\t\n    93\t;; =============================================================================\n    94\t;; Process A: one served ring buffer behind two endpoints\n    95\t;; =============================================================================\n    96\t\n    97\t(defn- make-endpoint-composition\n    98\t  \"Compose one serving endpoint over `source`, with `slot-count` capacity-one\n    99\t   acceptance-handoff slots.  One slot would make fact 3 a race against the\n   100\t   driver's cadence rather than a test of attachment identity.\"\n   101\t  [source path slot-count]\n   102\t  (let [descriptor (table-descriptor path)\n   103\t        control (buffer)\n   104\t        slots (vec (repeatedly slot-count (fn [] {:offer (buffer 1) :ack (buffer 1)})))\n   105\t        endpoint (ws/make-endpoint\n   106\t                   {:served {path descriptor}\n   107\t                    :control {:dao.stream/handle control :dao.stream/surface #{:writer}}\n   108\t                    :control-admission admission\n   109\t                    :slots (mapv (fn [{:keys [offer ack]}]\n   110\t                                   {:offer {:dao.stream/handle offer\n   111\t                                            :dao.stream/surface #{:writer}}\n   112\t                                    :offer-admission handoff-admission\n   113\t                                    :ack {:dao.stream/handle ack\n   114\t                                          :dao.stream/surface #{:writer}}\n   115\t                                    :ack-admission handoff-admission\n   116\t                                    :ack-cursor (newest ack)})\n   117\t                                 slots)\n   118\t                    :expiry-ms nil})\n   119\t        media (atom {})\n   120\t        listener (atom nil)\n   121\t        composition\n   122\t        (serving/make-serving\n   123\t          {:endpoint endpoint\n   124\t           :served {path {:descriptor descriptor :stream source}}\n   125\t           :control-reader control\n   126\t           :control-cursor (newest control)\n   127\t           :slots (mapv (fn [{:keys [offer ack]}]\n   128\t                          {:offer-reader offer\n   129\t                           :offer-cursor (newest offer)\n   130\t                           :ack-writer {:dao.stream/handle ack\n   131\t                                        :dao.stream/surface #{:writer}}})\n   132\t                        slots)\n   133\t           ;; Newest rather than the default oldest: an attachment observes\n   134\t           ;; what is appended after it joined, so one fact's appends cannot\n   135\t           ;; be replayed into another fact's attachment.\n   136\t           :forward-anchor stream/anchor-newest\n   137\t           :forward-options {:batch-budget 16 :gap-policy :terminate}\n   138\t           :make-traffic (fn [offer-event]\n   139\t                           (let [traffic (buffer)]\n   140\t                             (swap! media assoc (:ws/attachment offer-event) traffic)\n   141\t                             {:traffic {:dao.stream/handle traffic\n   142\t                                        :dao.stream/surface #{:writer}}\n   143\t                              :admission admission\n   144\t                              :reader traffic\n   145\t                              :cursor (newest traffic)}))\n   146\t           ;; No `:inbound-step`: inbound payload stays ordinary traffic data\n   147\t           ;; on the per-attachment medium and is deliberately not interpreted\n   148\t           ;; into appends on the served stream.\n   149\t           :start-endpoint! (fn [ep]\n   150\t                              (reset! listener (node/listen! ep {:host \"127.0.0.1\"\n   151\t                                                                 :port 0}))\n   152\t                              {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok})\n   153\t           :stop-endpoint! (fn [_]\n   154\t                             (node/stop-listening! @listener)\n   155\t                             {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok})})]\n   156\t    {:path path\n   157\t     :descriptor descriptor\n   158\t     :composition composition\n   159\t     :media media\n   160\t     :listener listener}))\n   161\t\n   162\t\n   163\t(defn- server-fixture\n   164\t  []\n   165\t  (let [source (buffer)]\n   166\t    {:source source\n   167\t     :primary (make-endpoint-composition source \"/slice\" 4)\n   168\t     :secondary (make-endpoint-composition source \"/slice-b\" 4)}))\n   169\t\n   170\t\n   171\t(defn- reachable\n   172\t  \"Repair a served descriptor's reachability from the bound port.  This is the\n   173\t   value that crosses to B as text, and the only thing B ever learns about A.\"\n   174\t  [endpoint]\n   175\t  (assoc (:descriptor endpoint) :ws/port (node/listener-port @(:listener endpoint))))\n   176\t\n   177\t\n   178\t;; =============================================================================\n   179\t;; Waiting, as promises over the event loop\n   180\t;; =============================================================================\n   181\t\n   182\t(defn- poll-until\n   183\t  \"Resolve with the first truthy value `pred` returns, or reject at the\n   184\t   deadline.  Polling is the only honest wait here: no operation blocks, and\n   185\t   nothing notifies.\"\n   186\t  [pred timeout-ms message]\n   187\t  (js/Promise.\n   188\t    (fn [resolve reject]\n   189\t      (let [deadline (+ (js/Date.now) timeout-ms)]\n   190\t        (letfn [(tick []\n   191\t                  (let [value (try (pred) (catch :default _ nil))]\n   192\t                    (cond\n   193\t                      value (resolve value)\n   194\t                      (< deadline (js/Date.now)) (reject (js/Error. message))\n   195\t                      :else (js/setTimeout tick 10))))]\n   196\t          (tick))))))\n   197\t\n   198\t\n   199\t;; =============================================================================\n   200\t;; Process B: a real child process, spoken to only over pipes\n   201\t;; =============================================================================\n   202\t\n   203\t(defn- line-reader\n   204\t  \"Collect whole newline-terminated lines out of a Node stream's chunks.\"\n   205\t  [readable on-line]\n   206\t  (let [pending (atom \"\")]\n   207\t    (.setEncoding ^js readable \"utf8\")\n   208\t    (.on ^js readable \"data\"\n   209\t         (fn [chunk]\n   210\t           (let [parts (str/split (str @pending chunk) #\"\\n\" -1)]\n   211\t             (reset! pending (last parts))\n   212\t             (doseq [line (butlast parts)\n   213\t                     :when (not (str/blank? line))]\n   214\t               (on-line line)))))))\n   215\t\n   216\t\n   217\t(defn- start-peer!\n   218\t  [descriptor]\n   219\t  (let [process (.spawn child-process \"node\"\n   220\t                        #js [peer-script (transit/encode-descriptor descriptor)]\n   220\t                        #js [peer-script (transit/encode-descriptor descriptor)]\n   221\t                        #js {:stdio #js [\"pipe\" \"pipe\" \"pipe\"]})\n   222\t        replies (atom [])\n   223\t        errors (atom [])]\n   224\t    ;; Loading B's namespaces may print to B's stdout before the peer protocol\n   225\t    ;; starts, so a line that is not a Transit reply is noise rather than a\n   226\t    ;; protocol failure: recording it and carrying on keeps one banner from\n   227\t    ;; silently stopping the reader.\n   228\t    (line-reader (.-stdout process)\n   229\t                 (fn [line]\n   230\t                   (let [reply (try (transit/decode line) (catch :default _ nil))]\n   231\t                     (if (:reply reply)\n   232\t                       (swap! replies conj reply)\n   233\t                       (swap! errors conj line)))))\n   234\t    (line-reader (.-stderr process) (fn [line] (swap! errors conj line)))\n   235\t    {:process process :replies replies :errors errors :seen (atom [])}))\n   236\t\n   237\t\n   238\t(defn- stop-peer!\n   239\t  [peer]\n   240\t  (try (.kill ^js (:process peer)) (catch :default _ nil)))\n   241\t\n   242\t\n   243\t(defn- take-reply!\n   244\t  \"Consume the first reply of `kind`.\"\n   245\t  [peer kind]\n   246\t  (poll-until\n   247\t    (fn []\n   248\t      (when-let [index (first (keep-indexed (fn [i r] (when (= kind (:reply r)) i))\n   249\t                                            @(:replies peer)))]\n   250\t        (let [reply (nth @(:replies peer) index)]\n   251\t          (swap! (:replies peer)\n   252\t                 (fn [rs] (vec (concat (subvec rs 0 index) (subvec rs (inc index))))))\n   253\t          reply)))\n   254\t    reply-ms\n   255\t    (str \"process B never replied \" kind \"; its other output was \"\n   256\t         (pr-str @(:errors peer)))))\n   257\t\n   258\t\n   259\t(defn- ask!\n   260\t  [peer command kind]\n   261\t  (.write ^js (.-stdin ^js (:process peer)) (str (transit/encode command) \"\\n\"))\n   262\t  (take-reply! peer kind))\n   263\t\n   264\t\n   265\t(defn- poll-events!\n   266\t  \"Ask B for whatever its medium has accumulated since B last reported, and\n   267\t   remember it.  B advances only its own kept cursor; A never touches it.\"\n   268\t  [peer]\n   269\t  (.then (ask! peer {:cmd :events} :events)\n   270\t         (fn [reply]\n   271\t           (swap! (:seen peer) into (:events reply))\n   272\t           @(:seen peer))))\n   273\t\n   274\t\n   275\t(defn- await-event\n   276\t  [peer pred message]\n   277\t  (let [deadline (+ (js/Date.now) event-ms)]\n   278\t    (js/Promise.\n   279\t      (fn [resolve reject]\n   280\t        (letfn [(tick []\n   281\t                  (.then (poll-events! peer)\n   282\t                         (fn [seen]\n   283\t                           (if-let [hit (first (filter pred seen))]\n   284\t                             (resolve hit)\n   285\t                             (if (< deadline (js/Date.now))\n   286\t                               (reject (js/Error. message))\n   287\t                               (js/setTimeout tick 20))))\n   288\t                         reject))]\n   289\t          (tick))))))\n   290\t\n   291\t\n   292\t(defn- attach-peer!\n   293\t  \"Spawn B, wait for its bootstrap, attach, and wait for the opened event.\"\n   294\t  [peers descriptor]\n   295\t  (let [peer (start-peer! descriptor)]\n   296\t    (swap! peers conj peer)\n   297\t    (-> (take-reply! peer :ready)\n   298\t        (.then (fn [ready]\n   299\t                 (is (= descriptor (:descriptor ready))\n   300\t                     \"the descriptor B decoded from text differs from the one A encoded\")\n   301\t                 (ask! peer {:cmd :attach} :attach)))\n   302\t        (.then (fn [attach]\n   303\t                 (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:outcome attach)))\n   304\t                 (.then (await-event peer #(= :ws/opened (:ws/event %))\n   305\t                                     \"the attachment never opened\")\n   306\t                        (fn [_] (assoc peer :attachment (:attachment attach)))))))))\n   307\t\n   308\t\n   309\t(defn- server-attachment\n   310\t  \"Correlate B to the server-side session it joined by the token it appended.\n   311\t   The two sides mint their own attachment identities, so nothing but a\n   312\t   payload can connect them — which is itself worth asserting.\"\n   313\t  [endpoint token]\n   314\t  (poll-until\n   315\t    (fn []\n   316\t      (first (first (filter (fn [[_ medium]]\n   317\t                              (some #(= token (:ws/value %)) (drain medium)))\n   318\t                            @(:media endpoint)))))\n   319\t    event-ms\n   320\t    \"A never received B's outbound payload\"))\n   321\t\n   322\t\n   323\t(defn- run-slice\n   324\t  \"Start process A, run one fact, then tear everything down exactly once.\"\n   325\t  [done body]\n   326\t  (let [fixture (server-fixture)\n   327\t        peers (atom [])]\n   328\t    (serving/start! (:composition (:primary fixture)))\n   329\t    (serving/start! (:composition (:secondary fixture)))\n   330\t    (let [ticker (js/setInterval\n   331\t                   (fn []\n   332\t                     (let [now (js/Date.now)]\n   333\t                       (serving/step! (:composition (:primary fixture)) now)\n   334\t                       (serving/step! (:composition (:secondary fixture)) now)))\n   335\t                   5)\n   336\t          teardown (fn []\n   337\t                     (js/clearInterval ticker)\n   338\t                     (doseq [peer @peers] (stop-peer! peer))\n   339\t                     (serving/stop! (:composition (:primary fixture)))\n   340\t                     (serving/stop! (:composition (:secondary fixture))))]\n   341\t      (-> (poll-until #(and (node/listener-port @(:listener (:primary fixture)))\n   342\t                            (node/listener-port @(:listener (:secondary fixture))))\n   343\t                      bind-ms\n   344\t                      \"the listeners never reported bound ports\")\n   345\t          (.then (fn [_] (body fixture peers)))\n   346\t          (.then (fn [_] nil)\n   347\t                 (fn [error] (is false (str \"slice failure: \" (.-message ^js error)))))\n   348\t          (.then (fn [_] (teardown) (done)))))))\n   349\t\n   350\t\n   351\t;; =============================================================================\n   352\t;; The five facts\n   353\t;; =============================================================================\n   354\t\n   355\t(deftest detachment-is-observable-on-both-sides\n   356\t  ;; Fact 1.\n   357\t  (async done\n   358\t    (run-slice\n   359\t      done\n   360\t      (fn [{:keys [source primary]} peers]\n   361\t        (let [me (atom nil)\n   362\t              token (atom nil)\n   363\t              attachment (atom nil)]\n   364\t          (-> (attach-peer! peers (reachable primary))\n   365\t              (.then (fn [peer]\n   366\t                       (reset! me peer)\n   367\t                       (reset! token [:slice/fact-1 (:attachment peer)])\n   368\t                       (ask! peer {:cmd :append :value :slice/established} :append)))\n   369\t              (.then (fn [reply]\n   370\t                       (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:outcome reply))\n   371\t                           \"an established attachment must accept an outbound append\")\n   372\t                       (ask! @me {:cmd :append :value @token} :append)))\n   373\t              (.then (fn [reply]\n   374\t                       (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:outcome reply)))\n   375\t                       (server-attachment primary @token)))\n   376\t              (.then (fn [server-side]\n   377\t                       (reset! attachment server-side)\n   378\t                       ;; Kill the connection from B's side.\n   379\t                       (ask! @me {:cmd :close} :close)))\n   380\t              (.then (fn [reply]\n   381\t                       (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:outcome reply)))\n   382\t                       (ask! @me {:cmd :append :value :after-close} :append)))\n   383\t              (.then (fn [reply]\n   384\t                       (testing \"B's handle answers closed\"\n   385\t                         (is (= :dao.stream/closed (:outcome reply))))\n   386\t                       (await-event @me #(= :ws/closed (:ws/event %))\n   387\t                                    \"B's own medium never received the terminal event\")))\n   388\t              (.then (fn [_]\n   389\t                       (poll-until\n   390\t                         #(= :ws/closed (:ws/event (last (drain (get @(:media primary)\n   391\t                                                                    @attachment)))))\n   392\t                         event-ms\n   393\t                         \"A's per-attachment medium never deposited the departure\")))\n   394\t              (.then (fn [_]\n   395\t                       (testing \"A's boundary deposits the departure\"\n   396\t                         (is (not (contains? (:sessions (serving/state (:composition primary)))\n   397\t                                             @attachment))\n   398\t                             \"the driver kept a session for a departed attachment\"))\n   399\t                       (testing \"the served stream is untouched by a connection's death\"\n   400\t                         (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome\n   401\t                                                 (stream/append! source :slice/still-alive)))))))))))))\n   402\t\n   403\t\n   404\t(deftest the-same-descriptor-rejoins-the-same-logical-stream\n   405\t  ;; Fact 2.\n   406\t  (async done\n   407\t    (run-slice\n   408\t      done\n   409\t      (fn [{:keys [source primary]} peers]\n   410\t        (let [me (atom nil)\n   411\t              first-attachment (atom nil)\n   412\t              again (atom nil)\n   413\t              token (atom nil)]\n   414\t          (-> (attach-peer! peers (reachable primary))\n   415\t              (.then (fn [peer]\n   416\t                       (reset! me peer)\n   417\t                       (reset! first-attachment (:attachment peer))\n   418\t                       (ask! peer {:cmd :close} :close)))\n   419\t              (.then (fn [reply]\n   420\t                       (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:outcome reply)))\n   421\t                       (await-event @me #(= :ws/closed (:ws/event %))\n   422\t                                    \"the attachment never closed\")))\n   423\t              ;; The identical bootstrapped descriptor value, reused verbatim.\n   424\t              (.then (fn [_] (ask! @me {:cmd :attach} :attach)))\n   425\t              (.then (fn [reply]\n   426\t                       (reset! again (:attachment reply))\n   427\t                       (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:outcome reply))\n   428\t                           \"reattachment with the same descriptor was refused\")\n   429\t                       (is (not= @first-attachment @again)\n   430\t                           \"a reattachment is a new attachment, not a resurrected one\")\n   431\t                       (await-event @me\n   432\t                                    (fn [event]\n   433\t                                      (and (= :ws/opened (:ws/event event))\n   434\t                                           (= @again (:ws/attachment event))))\n   435\t                                    \"the reattachment never opened\")))\n   436\t              (.then (fn [_]\n   437\t                       (reset! token [:slice/fact-2 @again])\n   438\t                       ;; A appends to the surviving logical stream; the\n   439\t                       ;; rejoined attachment receives it, which is what \"same\n   440\t                       ;; logical stream\" means operationally.\n   441\t                       (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! source @token))))\n   442\t                       (await-event @me #(= @token (:ws/value %))\n   443\t                                    \"the rejoined attachment received nothing from the served stream\")))\n   444\t              (.then (fn [hit] (is (some? hit))))))))))\n   445\t\n   446\t\n   447\t(deftest simultaneous-attachments-carry-distinct-attachment-identity\n   448\t  ;; Fact 3.\n   449\t  (async done\n   450\t    (run-slice\n   451\t      done\n   452\t      (fn [{:keys [source primary]} peers]\n   453\t        (let [descriptor (reachable primary)\n   454\t              one (atom nil)\n   455\t              two (atom nil)]\n   456\t          (-> (attach-peer! peers descriptor)\n   457\t              (.then (fn [peer] (reset! one peer) (attach-peer! peers descriptor)))\n   458\t              (.then (fn [peer]\n   459\t                       (reset! two peer)\n   460\t                       (is (string? (:attachment @one)))\n   461\t                       (is (string? (:attachment @two)))\n   462\t                       (is (not= (:attachment @one) (:attachment @two))\n   463\t                           \"two simultaneous attachments shared one attachment identity\")\n   464\t                       (ask! @one {:cmd :append :value [:slice/fact-3 (:attachment @one)]}\n   465\t                             :append)))\n   466\t              (.then (fn [_]\n   467\t                       (ask! @two {:cmd :append :value [:slice/fact-3 (:attachment @two)]}\n   468\t                             :append)))\n   469\t              (.then (fn [_]\n   470\t                       (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome\n   471\t                                               (stream/append! source :slice/fanout))))\n   472\t                       (await-event @one #(= :slice/fanout (:ws/value %))\n   473\t                                    \"the first attachment received nothing\")))\n   474\t              (.then (fn [_] (await-event @two #(= :slice/fanout (:ws/value %))\n   475\t                                          \"the second attachment received nothing\")))\n   476\t              (.then (fn [_]\n   477\t                       (testing \"every event on a client medium carries that client's identity\"\n   478\t                         (doseq [peer [@one @two]]\n   479\t                           (let [events @(:seen peer)]\n   480\t                             (is (seq events))\n   481\t                             (is (every? #(= (:attachment peer) (:ws/attachment %)) events)\n   482\t                   