ter retaining its next cursors.\"\n   470\t  [endpoint now]\n   471\t  ;; A pending connection can be lost before any acknowledgement: the peer\n   472\t  ;; closes, the wire protocol fails, or its own handle is closed.  Each of\n   473\t  ;; those paths closes the handle's state and deposits its terminal event;\n   474\t  ;; this is where the endpoint observes that and returns the slot, so bounded\n   475\t  ;; admission is a live bound rather than a monotonically shrinking one.\n   476\t  (doseq [[index slot] (map-indexed vector (:slots (endpoint-state endpoint)))\n   477\t          :when (and (= :pending (:status slot))\n   478\t                     (= :closed (:phase @(:handle-state slot))))]\n   479\t    (release-slot! endpoint index (:attachment slot)))\n   480\t  (doseq [[index slot] (map-indexed vector (:slots (endpoint-state endpoint)))\n   481\t          :when (= :pending (:status slot))]\n   482\t    (let [next (stream/next (:dao.stream/handle (:ack slot)) (:ack-cursor slot))]\n   483\t      (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome next))\n   484\t        (swap! (:state endpoint) assoc-in [:slots index :ack-cursor] (:dao.stream/cursor next))\n   485\t        (let [ack (:dao.stream/value next)]\n   486\t          (cond\n   487\t            (not= (:attachment slot) (:ws/attachment ack)) nil\n   488\t            (valid-ack? ack (:attachment slot)) (accept-slot! endpoint index slot ack)\n   489\t            :else (let [hstate (:handle-state slot)]\n   490\t                    (swap! hstate assoc :phase :closed)\n   491\t                    (invoke-close! (:socket @hstate) protocol-close-code \"dao.stream/invalid-ack\")\n   492\t                    (terminal! hstate (:attachment slot) :ws/closed)\n   493\t                    (release-slot! endpoint index (:attachment slot))))))))\n   494\t  ;; Expiry is deliberately clock-domain explicit.  An endpoint composition\n   495\t  ;; may set `:opened-at` when it accepts an offer; this transport does not\n   496\t  ;; invent wall-clock time or a scheduler.\n   497\t  (when-let [expiry (:expiry-ms (:config endpoint))]\n   498\t    (doseq [[index slot] (map-indexed vector (:slots (endpoint-state endpoint)))\n   499\t            :when (and (= :pending (:status slot)) (:opened-at slot)\n   500\t                       (<= (+ (:opened-at slot) expiry) now))]\n   501\t      (let [hstate (:handle-state slot)]\n   502\t        (swap! hstate assoc :phase :closed)\n   503\t        (invoke-close! (:socket @hstate) 1000 \"dao.stream/acceptance-expired\")\n   504\t        (terminal! hstate (:attachment slot) :ws/closed)\n   505\t        (release-slot! endpoint index (:attachment slot)))))\n   506\t  endpoint)\ndocs/design/dao.stream.ws.md:9:A WebSocket descriptor names a **server-hosted stream**, never a connection.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.ws.md:15:honest here: the same descriptor reaches the same stream every time, because\ndocs/design/dao.stream.ws.md:16:the stream's identity and lifecycle belong to the server, not to the wire.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.ws.md:21:that ring buffer; the endpoint produces a descriptor carrying its address and\ndocs/design/dao.stream.ws.md:22:the ring buffer's unchanged logical-stream identity, and remote\ndocs/design/dao.stream.ws.md:24:the host composed, which is exactly the contract's rule that descriptors\ndocs/design/dao.stream.ws.md:30:stream's descriptor.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.ws.md:34:A WebSocket handle is **writer** and **closable**, plus `descriptor` as every\ndocs/design/dao.stream.ws.md:40:`descriptor` with reachability for the endpoint through which they attached\ndocs/design/dao.stream.ws.md:41:and with the served stream's transport-independent `:dao.stream/identity`.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.ws.md:42:Two endpoints may therefore produce different descriptors for the same served\ndocs/design/dao.stream.ws.md:43:stream, while every such result carries the same identity.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.ws.md:44:`:dao.stream/attachment` distinguishes connec